{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":30151810,"ns":0,"title":"Dyadic cubes","extract":"In mathematics, the dyadic cubes are a collection of cubes in Rn of different sizes or scales such that the set of cubes of each scale partition Rn and each cube in one scale may be written as a union of cubes of a smaller scale. These are frequently used in mathematics (particularly harmonic analysis) as a way of discretizing objects in order to make computations or analysis easier.","description":"Hypercube partition of Euclidean space","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}